  "publicacion": {
    "titulo": "Warren Buffett's 5-minute fix for the deficit",
    "descripcion": "In a live CNBC interview on July 7, 2011, Warren Buffett said he could end the deficit in five minutes: pass a law that any time the deficit tops 3% of GDP, all sitting members of Congress are ineligible for re-election. He said it with a laugh, and Berkshire Hathaway later called it not a serious proposal, just a point about incentives. In fiscal 2026 the federal deficit was $1.99 trillion (Monthly Treasury Statement, September 2026), about 6.2% of GDP by CRFB's estimate. Not financial advice. Sources: CNBC, October 2011; U.S. Treasury Monthly Treasury Statement, Sept 2026; Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget, Oct 1, 2026.",
